4. Diastolic blood pressure should be ≤60 mmHg (8.0 kPa) in at least 5% of subjects;
5. Diastolic blood pressure should be ≥100 mmHg (13.33 kPa) in at least 5% of subjects; (f) At least 20% of subjects should have a diastolic blood pressure ≥85 mmHg (11.33 kPa);
5. Subjects must be willing and able to comply with the study procedures by signing an informed consent form after being informed about the study.

consent form after understanding the contents of the study.
